    145	| Differentiable programming for π(x) (DARTS architecture search) | USED I (S216, edge E2.33) — depth-3 differentiable circuit on (n, χ_P(n)) at N=12 with gate library {AND, OR, XOR, MAJ_3/5/7, ID, NOT}, soft-input selection via sigmoid logits β, gate-temperature anneal τ ≈ 2 → 10. PRIMES converges deterministically to 1-bit oddness floor (final BCE 0.2969 ± 0.0000 ≈ 0.2961 baseline) across 3 seeds. Matched-density random control plateaus at entropy floor 0.3967 ± 0.0113. Calibrated-1-bit control (parity-conditional density matched) at 0.2963 ± 0.0004 — statistically indistinguishable from PRIMES (Welch t = +2.3, p = 0.14). Argmax discretisation collapses to constant-zero (MAJ_k with empty selected set); discrete accuracy = majority-class baseline at every n-window (train, [2^N, 2^N+1000), [10^5, 10^5+1000)) — known DARTS failure mode (Zela et al. ICLR 2020). Cross-domain technique survives import but signal fully reduces to S84's oddness mechanism. **Adds 36th orthogonal pseudorandomness measure** with same elementary mechanism as S84 (oddness mod 2). | Liu-Simonyan-Yang 2019 "DARTS: Differentiable Architecture Search" ICLR 2019 = arXiv:1806.09055 https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.09055; Bender-Kindermans-Zoph-Vasudevan-Le 2018 "Understanding and Simplifying One-Shot Architecture Search" ICML 2018; Zela-Elsken-Saikia-Marrakchi-Brox-Hutter 2020 "Understanding and Robustifying Differentiable Architecture Search" ICLR 2020 = arXiv:1909.09656 https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.09656; Baydin-Pearlmutter-Radul-Siskind 2018 "Automatic Differentiation in Machine Learning: a Survey" JMLR 18 | D8 (CLOSED S216 — DARTS depth-3 PRIMES advantage = oddness only; calibrated-1-bit indistinguishable from PRIMES at p=0.14; argmax discretisation lossy → discrete circuit = constant zero; cross-domain DARTS import is mode-I) |
